<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia Feb merchandise imports A$6.098 bln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia Feb merchandise imports A$6.098 bln.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's international merchandise imports stood at A$6.098 billion in February from a reported A$6.423 billion in January, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>This measure is compiled from information submitted by importers or their agents to the Australian customs service. It is not seasonally adjusted nor is it reported on the same balance of payments basis as monthly current account data.</p>
<p>This new measure takes the place of former merchandise imports figures which are now included in a monthly merchandise trade balance series.</p>
<p>    IMPORTS					   Feb		Jan</p>
<p>Food, live animals			    238 million    279 million</p>
<p>Beverages, tobacco			     35 million     38 million</p>
<p>Crude materials, except fuels	     119 million    113 million</p>
<p>Mineral fuels, related materials	  492 million    518 million</p>
<p>Animal, vegetable oils, fats		 20 million     20 million</p>
<p>Chemical and related products	     712 million    768 million</p>
<p>Manufactured goods			    848 million    907 million</p>
<p>Machinery and transport			 2.619 bln	2.845 bln</p>
<p>Miscellaneous manufactured		  962 million    877 million</p>
<p>Commodities and transactions</p>
<p>not classified elsewhere		     53 million     58 million</p>
<p>Total Imports				     6.098 bln	6.423 bln</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
